sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: docs/reference/tasks.md, explicit review parking; flow-tighten rule 14. The canonical provider child checks the stopped state; the Gateway retains admitted IDs.
  %% status: migrated
  %% command: task:park
  %% kind: tasks.park
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as VM provider<br/>Incus
  CLI->>GW: task:park 42
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit task:park 42 --idempotency-key=park-1`
  %%> - syntax: `<task> [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  Note over GW: Admit review parking<br/>group 42 · owned VM
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the external group has an open published PR, and every subtask is ended or still `todo`
  %%> - a `todo` subtask is parked only when no turn, check or prep run of the group is running; a prep run leaves its spec subtask `todo` because the code follows
  %%> - a subtask that runs or waits for review still refuses the park
  %%> - the group has no active execution, assistance or preview
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to the serving Node
  %%> Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review:
  %%> - the workspace lease is gone, so the park no longer checks for a held lease; the group's Operation lock already refuses a busy group
  GW->>SW: Start one run<br/>operation-task-park
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the admitted group, Project, Instance, VM and provider identity
  %%> - SSH host pins for Incus
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>Operation recorded
  %%> Result:
  %%> - follow the Operation while Swamp stops the owned VM
  Note over SW: eligible
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - native assert retains the admission eligibility check before provider work
  SW->>N: provider
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - run the canonical provider stop action and check the stopped state
  %%> - an already stopped VM completes without another stop
  %%> - no script prints the admitted IDs or a second completion report
  alt provider confirmed stopped
    SW-->>GW: Native terminal result<br/>provider succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the same history read confirms the provider child succeeded
    Note over GW: Record the parked VM<br/>waiting for review
    %%> Result:
    %%> - record the admitted IDs and stop confirmation; keep the workspace and PR
  else stop failed or interrupted
    N--xSW: Stop unconfirmed
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the provider child retains the native failure
    SW--xGW: Native failed result<br/>failed step · error code
    %%> Result:
    %%> - retain the VM and group without recording a stop confirmation
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - inspect the failed provider action before admitting another park
  end
  loop until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show<br/>Operation number
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the Operation status and stop confirmation
  end
